WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:03.728
FILIBUSTER IN THE SENATE.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.196
DOUG McKELWAY TELLS US TONIGHT

00:00:03.861 --> 00:00:07.131
IT'S A ROAD WE AS A COUNTRY HAVE

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:09.734
BEEN DONE BEFORE.

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:12.403
&gt;&gt; TONIGHT I ASK YOU TO GIVE ME

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:15.907
WHAT 43 GOVERNORS ALREADY HAVE

00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:17.742
GIVEN ME, A LINE ITEM VETO.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.776
&gt;&gt; GENERATIONS OF PRESIDENTS

00:00:17.875 --> 00:00:20.545
WANTED A LINE ITEM VETO.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.345
NONE HAD IT UNTIL THE CLINTON

00:00:20.678 --> 00:00:24.649
ADMINISTRATION WHEN CONGRESS

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:24.949
PASSED THE LINE ITEM VETO ACT OF

00:00:24.782 --> 00:00:27.485
1996.

00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:28.953
CLINTON USED IT 82 TIMES BEFORE

00:00:27.618 --> 00:00:29.587
THE SUPREME COURT RULED IT

00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:29.887
UNCONSTITUTIONAL TWO YEARS

00:00:29.721 --> 00:00:31.756
LATER.

00:00:30.021 --> 00:00:32.790
THAT DIDN'T STOP FUTURE

00:00:31.889 --> 00:00:34.759
PRESIDENTS FROM WANTING IT.

00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:35.526
&gt;&gt; I THINK THERE IS NOT A

00:00:34.892 --> 00:00:37.028
PRESIDENT OUT THERE WHO WOULDN'T

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.463
LOVE TO HAVE IT.

00:00:37.161 --> 00:00:39.864
&gt;&gt; INCLUDING PRESIDENT TRUMP WHO

00:00:38.596 --> 00:00:45.103
IS FRUSTRATED AT THE DEMOCRATIC

00:00:39.997 --> 00:00:46.971
LEVERAGE IN THE SPENDING BILL.

00:00:45.236 --> 00:00:47.338
IT GAVE TAXPAYERS MORE DEFICIT

00:00:47.105 --> 00:00:48.039
SPENDING.

00:00:47.472 --> 00:00:53.344
&gt;&gt; I'M CALLING ON CONGRESS TO

00:00:48.172 --> 00:00:54.512
GIVE ME A LINE ITEM VETO FOR ALL

00:00:53.478 --> 00:00:55.546
GOVERNMENT SPENDING BILLS.

00:00:54.645 --> 00:00:56.948
&gt;&gt; TREASURY SECRETARY STATEMENT

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.050
AGAIN REPEATED THE PRESIDENT'S

00:00:57.081 --> 00:00:59.717
CALL ON SUNDAY, PAYING NO HEED

00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.352
TO ITS UNCONSTITUTIONALITY.

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:06.958
&gt;&gt; I THINK THEY SHOULD GIVE THE

00:01:01.486 --> 00:01:09.660
PRESIDENT A LINE ITEM VETO.

00:01:07.091 --> 00:01:09.494
&gt;&gt; RULED UNCONSTITUTIONAL BY   B

00:01:09.494 --> 00:01:09.527
&gt;&gt; RULED UNCONSTITUTIONAL BY   Y

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:09.560
&gt;&gt; RULED UNCONSTITUTIONAL BY   T

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.128
&gt;&gt; RULED UNCONSTITUTIONAL BY   E

00:01:09.794 --> 00:01:11.596
SUPREME COURT'S.

00:01:10.261 --> 00:01:13.030
&gt;&gt; CONGRESS CAN PASS A RULE THAT

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:15.099
ALLOWS THEM TO DO IT.

00:01:13.164 --> 00:01:17.335
&gt;&gt; IT WOULD TAKE A

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:19.003
CONSTITUTIONAL AMENDMENT.

00:01:17.468 --> 00:01:19.871
CONGRESS TRIED IN 2011 AFTER THE

00:01:19.137 --> 00:01:21.372
HIGH COURT RULING.

00:01:20.004 --> 00:01:23.141
IT TINKERED WITH A MORE MODERN

00:01:21.506 --> 00:01:24.776
VERSION OF A LINE ITEM VETO THAT

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:25.276
ATTEMPTED TO MAINTAIN THE

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:27.378
BALANCE OF POWER.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:28.813
&gt;&gt; THE PRESIDENT WOULD PROPOSE

00:01:27.512 --> 00:01:29.714
CUTS AND CONGRESS WOULD HAVE TO

00:01:28.946 --> 00:01:30.515
APPROVE THOSE CUTS.

00:01:29.847 --> 00:01:33.785
THE PRESIDENT COULDN'T GO IN AND

00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:36.921
STRIKE EVERYTHING HE WANTED.

00:01:33.918 --> 00:01:37.488
&gt;&gt; THAT BILL DIED IN THE SENATE.

00:01:37.054 --> 00:01:37.955
WHERE DOES IT LEAVE

00:01:37.622 --> 00:01:40.358
PRESIDENT TRUMP?

00:01:38.089 --> 00:01:40.725
&gt;&gt; HE WANTS TO FIX THE BUDGET

00:01:40.491 --> 00:01:41.993
PROCESS.

00:01:40.858 --> 00:01:43.961
HIS MESSAGE TO LEADERS IN

00:01:42.126 --> 00:01:44.762
CONGRESS IN BOTH PARTIES IS THAT

00:01:44.095 --> 00:01:46.364
IF SOMETHING SIMILAR HAPPENS

00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:46.998
AGAIN, IS MUCH MORE INCLINED TO

00:01:46.497 --> 00:01:48.399
VETO IT.

00:01:47.131 --> 00:01:49.734
&gt;&gt; LOOK OUT FOR SEPTEMBER 30,

00:01:48.533 --> 00:01:51.969
THE DATE THE CURRENT FUNDING

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:53.671
BILL RUNS OUT IN THE PROCESS

